# README Requirements

Keep `README.md` user-focused. Align with `project-overview.mdc` and `implementation.mdc`.

## Required sections (order)

1. **Title & description** — GNU `tail`-compatible (matches GNU coreutils
   `tail` 9.4 except follow mode); prints the last part of files or stdin
   (default last 10 lines); raw `read(2)` / `write(2)` I/O; seeks from the end
   on regular files; no follow mode. List versions: v1.0.0 (POSIX-style
   subset, git tag) and v2.0.0 (current, GNU-compatible).

2. **Build**
   - `make`, `make debug`, `make test`, `make clean`, optional `make install`
   - Artefacts: **`build/tail-toto`**, **`build/tail-toto-debug`**,
     **`build/tests/test_core`**; mention `build/.gitkeep` / `build/tests/.gitkeep`
   - **Linux / WSL:** `make clean && make && make test` then `./build/tail-toto file`
   - **Windows:** Git Bash or MSYS2 **UCRT64**; `pacman -S make mingw-w64-ucrt-x86_64-gcc`
   - Explain Makefile **`<io.h>` probe**: POSIX vs Win32 binary-mode I/O; UCRT64 `gcc` on `PATH`
   - Native Windows `.exe` under `build/` runs in UCRT64, Git Bash, cmd, PowerShell

3. **Usage**
   - Show invocations as `./build/tail-toto` (or installed `tail-toto`)
   - `tail-toto [OPTION]... [FILE]...`; no `FILE` or `-` → stdin
   - Options table: `-n` / `--lines` and `-c` / `--bytes` with `NUM` and
     `+NUM`; `-q` / `--quiet` / `--silent`, `-v` / `--verbose`; `-z` /
     `--zero-terminated`; `--retry`, `--pid`, `-s` / `--sleep-interval`,
     `--max-unchanged-stats` (accepted, ignored without follow mode);
     `--help`, `--version`
   - NUM rules and multiplier suffix table; overflow is an error; sticky `+`
   - Obsolete syntax (`-5`, `+5`, `-3c`, `-2b`) and when it applies
   - Long-option prefixes (`--lin`, `--h`; `--v` ambiguous); options processed
     in order (first `--help` / `--version` wins); `-v` is verbose, `-h` invalid
   - Headers default on for multiple files; `-` is stdin; `--` ends options;
     `POSIXLY_CORRECT`
   - Unreadable files are reported and skipped; remaining files still print
   - "Differences from GNU tail" subsection: no follow mode (`-f` / `-F` /
     `--follow` rejected), `-5f` not recognized, `_POSIX2_VERSION` ignored, no
     `---presume-input-pipe`, own `--help` / `--version` text, `write error`
     wording, platform `<reason>` texts

4. **Exit codes**
   - `0`: success — all inputs processed (or `--help` / `--version`)
   - `1`: error — usage error, any unreadable input, or write failure
   - stderr: `tail-toto: <context>: <reason>` style diagnostics matching GNU wording

5. **Layout** — brief tree matching actual repo (include `LICENSE.txt`,
   `c_version.txt`, `build/.gitkeep`, `build/tests/.gitkeep`):
   - `include/tail_toto.h` + `tail_toto_{emit,cli,count,io,tail,run}.h`
   - `src/main.c` + `tail_toto_{emit,cli,count,io,tail,run}.c`
   - `tests/test_runner.c` + `test_*.c` → `build/tests/test_core`
   - Note that Windows builds skip pipe-based unit tests (`SKIP:`)

## Do not document in README

- Internal chain-of-thought comment blocks
- `-Werror` flag rationale (lives in `Makefile` comments)
- Author/licence banners on `--version` (binary prints `tail-toto <version>` only)
- Chunk-list / ring-buffer internals or `TAIL_TOTO_BUFSIZE`
- `find_long()`, `parse_obsolete()` or other static helper names unless briefly needed for contributors

## Style

- Fenced `sh` blocks for commands.
- No emojis unless the user asks.
- Keep prose minimal.
